            "text": "RTB · 2A DAILY INTEL · Thursday, August 6, 2026",
            "spacing": "None"
          },
          {
            "type": "TextBlock",
            "size": "Large",
            "weight": "Bolder",
            "text": "A federal judge just struck down most of the National Firearms Act — and gave the Justice Department one week to appeal.",
            "wrap": true,
            "spacing": "Small"
          },
          {
            "type": "TextBlock",
            "text": "No Aug 5 edition, so this covers 48 hours. On Aug 5, Judge James Wesley Hendrix (N.D. Tex.) permanently enjoined the NFA's regulatory provisions for untaxed firearms in Silencer Shop v. ATF, on taxing-power grounds only. He stayed it one week for DOJ to appeal, and relief runs only to the plaintiffs and their members and customers.",
            "wrap": true,
            "spacing": "Small"
          },
          {
            "type": "TextBlock",
            "size": "Small",
            "weight": "Bolder",
            "color": "Warning",
            "text": "HOTTEST LEADS",
            "spacing": "Medium"
          },
          {
            "type": "FactSet",
            "facts": [
              {
                "title": "1. Silencer Shop v. ATF — most of the NFA enjoined, stayed",
                "value": "Heat 95 ▲▲▲"
              },
              {
                "title": "2. Suppressor export transfer — NSSF conference final day",
                "value": "Heat 79 ▲▲"
              },
              {
                "title": "3. Viramontes/Grant — the reference clock",
                "value": "Heat 78 →"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "TextBlock",
            "size": "Small",
            "weight": "Bolder",
            "color": "Warning",
            "text": "WHAT'S MOVING",
            "spacing": "Medium"
          },
          {
            "type": "TextBlock",
            "size": "Small",
            "text": "• NFA enjoined as to plaintiffs — DOJ appeal window closes ~Aug 12 (T-6)\n• DOJ sued Montgomery County, MD Aug 3 over 100-yard carry exclusion zones\n• NSSF Import/Export Conference final day — suppressor asymmetry sharpened\n• ATF \"engaged in the business\" comment record closed Tuesday",
            "wrap": true
          }
